      "description": "Judgement methodologies the harness owns, one sub-graph each: Kepner-Tregoe for a decision, MADR for its record, DMN for the computable case. PARALLEL rather than composable — which applies is contextual, and blending them produces a house method that cites nobody. Its own graph typology rather than skills, for three properties a skill does not have: extractable (somebody else's work, adopted, so it lifts out with its declaration when the field moves on), referenced rather than inlined (two skills quoting one method is two copies free to drift), and exempt from skill criteria (skill-is-brief caps an INSTRUCTION near 280 lines; a methodology is a faithful rendering of an external standard, and truncating it to fit a house limit would misrepresent the standard). GRADE is deliberately NOT here: it is WHO guideline method, and since 2026-09-24 (bean `wg7r`) it is the `grade` skill in the DAK layer's `skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/` with its vocabularies as code lists — the owner: \"needs to be part of skill/SKOS etc. … dont want smart-kg here yet, that is its own repo already\". RELOCATION, 2026-09-22, and the THREE declarations it removed. The owner: \"dont bury sub-graph assets. same for <stub>/skills, etc.\" CRDM's three skills moved to `skills/sdlc/crdm/`, RACI's to `skills/process/raci/`, and CRDM's eight diagrams to `processes/` — the stub-level graphs that were already declared. `methodology-crdm`, `methodology-raci` and `methodology-crdm-processes` are GONE rather than repointed: a separate entry for a directory that is already a package subdirectory of the declared `skills/` graph would declare one directory twice, which is the `x4v4` graph-inside-a-graph shape one level down. `gen-skill-docs` demonstrated it rather than anyone reasoning it out — it demanded a category under BOTH the basename and the declaration id, because both discovery branches found the same directory. So this entry now has the `methodology` graph to itself, holding exactly the four nodes and no subgraph: dmn, kepner-tregoe, madr, swot. This REVERSES the placement half of bean `g43o`; its argument that a reader should meet CRDM as a thing rather than as three prefixed filenames is preserved by the package manifest, which is what makes a skill package a thing everywhere else in this tree.",
      "readmePath": "methodologies/README.md",
